# Files in this repo that Vercel must not upload.
#
# Vercel serves the repo root as the web root, so anything committed
# here is fetchable over HTTP unless it is listed below. That is fine
# for the pages and their scripts, which the browser needs anyway. It
# is not fine for the two things below.

# Edge Function source. These run on Supabase, not Vercel, so serving
# them achieves nothing -- and without this line the ai-assistant
# system prompt and all three functions' authorization logic would sit
# at https://<domain>/supabase/functions/<slug>/index.ts for anyone who
# guessed the path. They contain no secrets (every key comes from
# Deno.env), so this is not a breach waiting to happen; it is simply
# not the public's business, and there is no reason to publish it.
supabase/

# Local tooling. Node scripts that read and rewrite the repo. They are
# never fetched by a page and would only ever be served by accident.
sync-sri.js
sync-csp.js
sync-vendor.js
check-drift.js
build-clean.js

# The schema and its documentation. deploy-schema.sql is already kept
# out of the public repo by .gitignore; this is the belt to that
# braces, so a private-repo deploy does not quietly publish a full map
# of the database and its RLS policies at /deploy-schema.sql.
deploy-schema.sql
README.md
VERCEL.md
node_modules/
